    "chunk_text": "(i) to engage in any industry, trade or import and exportbusiness and to promote and carry on anyagricultural, industrial and commercial enterprise, toprovide aid and assistance to any person for suchenterprises, to conduct training programmes and toorganize services and propaganda campaigns, witha view to providing the public with technologicalexpertise;\n\n(j) to give aid by way of scholarships, or cash orotherwise, to monks, volunteers and other persons,engaged in the furtherance of the objects of theCorporation;\n\n3Mahanuwara Bauddha Vidya Peetaya(Incorporation) Act, No. 23 of 1999\n\n(l) to promote, arrange, organise and hold, exhibitions,lectures, seminars simposia, workshops, classesdebates, conferences, tours, excursions or otheractivities in furtherance of the objects of theCorporation;\n\n(m) to co-operate and associate with other associations,societies or organisations, having objects similar tothose of the Corporation;\n\n(n) to provide higher educational diplomas and othereducational programmes and courses of study inayurveda and indigenous medicine;\n\n(o) to act as an agent of any national or foreign technicalor vocational training institution or affiliate institutionor organization carrying on educational activities;\n\n(p) to do all other acts and things as are or may benecessary conducive, or incidental, to, theattainment of the above objects.\n\n4. Subject to the provisions of this Act, and other writtenlaw, the Corporation shall have the power to do, perform executeall such acts, matters and things whatsoever, as are necessaryor desirable for the promotion and furtherance of the objectsof the Corporation or any one of them, including the power toopen, operate and close bank accounts, to borrow or raisemoneys, with or without security, to receive or collect grantsand donations, to invest its funds, and to engage employ anddismiss officers and servants for the purpose of carrying outof the objects of the Corporation."
