    "chunk_text": "3Judicature (Amendment) Act, No. 27 of 1999\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nJUDICATURE (AMENDMENT)ACT, No. 27 OF 1999\n\n[Certified on 30th August, 1999]\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of September 03, 1999.\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA.TO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 1\n\nPrice: Rs. 3.50 Postage: Rs.3.50\n\n(Internet Version)\n\n1Judicature (Amendment) Act, No. 27 of 1999\n\n[Certified on 30th August , 1999]L.D. - O. 75/96.\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE JUDICATURE ACT, NO.2 OF 1978\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Judicature(Amendment) Act, No.27 of 1999.\n\n2.Section 48 of the Judicature Act, No. 2 of 1978, ishereby amended, by the repeal of the proviso to that sectionand the substitution therefor, of the following proviso :-\n\n\u201cProvided that where any criminal prosecution, proceeding or matter (except on an inquiry preliminary tocommittal for trial) is continued before the successor ofany such judge, the accused may demand that thewitnesses be resummoned and reheard.\u201d.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between theSinhala and Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala Text shallprevail\n\nShort title.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in case ofinconsistency.\n\nAmendment ofsection 48 of ActNo.2 of 1978\n\n2Payodunrata Development Foundation(Incorporation) Act, No.5 of 1999\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs.885 (Local). Rs.1,180 (Foreign),Payable to the SUPERINTENDENT. GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, No. 32, TRANSWORKS HOUSE,LOTUS ROAD, COLOMBO 01 before 15th December each year in respect of the year following."
