    "chunk_text": "(h) to establish vocational tranining centres andconduct training programmes with a view toproviding employment for youth ; and\n\n(i) to generally do all such acts and things as arenecessary for, or incidental or conducive to thecarrying out or the attainment of the objects of theCorporation.\n\nGeneral Powers ofthe Corporation.\n\n3Maitreya Buddha Dharmadutha Foundation(Incorporation) Act, No. 39 of 1999\n\nthe power to open operate and close bank accounts, borrowor raise the money with or without security, receive or collectgrants and donations, to invest its funds, enter into contractsand agreements and to engage, employ and dismiss officersand servants required for the carrying out of the objects ofthe Corporation.\n\n5. (1) The affairs of the Corporation shall, subject to therules of the Corporation be administered by a Board ofManagement elected in accordance with the rules of theCorporation.\n\n(2)The first Board of Management shall consist of theBoard of Directors of the Foundation holding office on theday immediately preceding the date of commencement of thisAct and whose names are set out in the Schedule to this Act.\n\n6. (1) It shall be lawful for the Corporation, from time totime at any general meeting of the members and by a majorityof not less than two- thirds of the members present andentitled to vote to make rules not inconsistent withprovisions of this Act or any other written law for theadmission , expulsion re withdrawal of members, for theelection of members of the Board of Management, for theconduct of the duties of the Board of Management and of thevarious officers, agents and servants of the Corporation forthe procedure to be followed in the transaction of business atmeetings of the Corporation and the Board of Managementand otherwise generally, for the management of the affairs ofthe Corporation and attainment of its objects. Such rules whenmay at a like meeting and in like manner, be altered, added to,amended or rescinded."
