    "chunk_size_bytes": 1925,
    "chunk_text": "(i) acquire by lease or otherwise, during the period forwhich the Competent Authority is appointed, anyproperty, rights or privileges that it considers necessaryfor exercising and discharging of its powers andfunctions ;\n\nCompetent Authority (Powers and Functions)Act, No. 3 of 20023\n\n(k) use the facilities and equipment belonging to the SriLanka Broadcasting Corporation or the Sri LankaRupavahini Corporation, as the case may be, in sucha manner as the Competent Authority considers fit forthe purpose of promoting and assisting any broadcastpertaining to an election or a referendum ;\n\n(l) during the period for which the Competent Authorityis appointed, take on lease or rent houses, sites anderect houses for the use of such officers and servantsappointed by such Authority ;\n\n(m) publish or arrange for the publication of suchperiodicals or other publications as it considersnecessary or beneficial ;\n\n(n) refuse to televise, record or broadcast anyadvertisement in any form, the televising, recordingor boardcasting of which is not in the public interest ;\n\n(o) act in combination or association with any person orbody of persons, whether incorporated orunincorporated, within Sri Lanka or abroad, in theexercise or discharge of the powers or functionsspecified in the section ; and\n\n(p) do all such acts or things which in the opinion of theCompetent Authority is necessary for the conduct ofa free and fair election or, a referendum, as the casemay be.\n\n3.In the exercise and discharge of the powers andfunctions under paragraphs (a), (b), (c), (d) and (e) of section2, it shall be the duty of the Competent Authority as far aspracticable, to be satisfied, that the programmes broadcast bythe Sri Lanka Broadcasting Corporation or the Sri LankaRupavahini Corporation as the case may be, comply with thefollowing conditions, in addition to any guidelines which theElection Commission may issue from time to time :\u2014"
