    "chunk_size_bytes": 1375,
    "chunk_text": "6.The Competent Authority and the officers and servantsappointed under section 5 of this Act, may be paid suchremuneration computed at such amount as may be determinedby the Election Commission which shall be a charge on theConsolidated Fund.\n\nSuit orprosecutionagainst theCompetentAuthority to beconsidered a suitor prosecutionagainst the State.\n\nOfficers andservants.\n\nRemuneration ofCompetentAuthority etc.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in case ofinconsistency.\n\nCompetent Authority (Powers and Functions)Act, No. 3 of 20025\n\n8.In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires\u2014\n\n\u201cbroadcasting\u201d means television or radio broadcast andincludes any signal, announcement, item,communication, picture or other matter to bebroadcast for reception by the public ;\n\n\u201cElection Commission\u201d means the Election Commissionestablished under Article 103 of the Constitution ;\n\n\u201cguidelines\u201d means the guidelines issued by the ElectionCommission under sub-paragraph (a) of paragraph(5) of Article 104B of the Constitution.\n\nInterpretation.\n\nCompetent Authority (Powers and Functions)Act, No. 3 of 20026\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs. 885 (Local), Rs. 1,180(Foreign),payable to the SUPERINTENDENT, GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, NO. 32, TRANSWORKS HOUSE,LOTUS ROAD, COLOMBO 01 before 15th December each year in respect of the year following."
