    "chunk_size_bytes": 2018,
    "chunk_text": "(5) The constitution of such Committees and the procedureto be adopted by such Committees shall be as prescribed.\n\nEstablishment ofthe Council of theYouth Corps.\n\nShort title.\n\n2\u2014H 016444 \u2014 5,550 (07/2002)\n\n2Youth Corps Act, No. 21 of 2002\n\n(a) youth development and employment training ; and\n\n(b) vocational education.\n\n4.The Council shall have the power\u2014\n\n(a) to prepare plans and programmes for the YouthCorps ;\n\n(b) to monitor and report on the implementation of suchplans and programmes prepared under paragraph (a),as are approved by the Minister ;\n\n(c) to supervise the training of the members of the YouthCorps ;\n\n(d) to specify in consultation with the Director of theYouth Corps, the conditions relating to the trainingand efficiency of the members of the Corps and thedegree of proficiency required to be attained by aranger.\n\nPART II\n\nYOUTH CORPS\n\n5.There shall be raised and Maintained, in accordancewith the provisions of this Act, a Corp to be known as theYouth Corps (hereinafter referred to as \u201cthe Corps\u201d).\n\n6.(1) The Corps shall be formed into such units andshall consist of such strength as the Minister may from timeto time determine.\n\n(2) The structure and ranks of the Corps and theappointments, promotions and demotions to and from, suchranks, shall be prescribed.\n\nObjectives of theYouth Corps.\n\nPowers of theCouncil.\n\nYouth Corps.\n\nMinister todetermine unitsstrengths ofCorps.\n\n3Youth Corps Act, No. 21 of 2002\n\n7.The Minister shall appoint a fit and proper person asthe Director of the Corps, who shall be responsible for theadministration, training, discipline and efficiency of theCorps.\n\n8.The Director of the Corps shall\u2014\n\n(a) give effect to the decisions of the Council and ensurethat the decisions of the Council are given effect to ;\n\n(b) furnish to the Council such information as it mayrequire for the exercise, performance and dischargeof its powers, duties and functions.\n\n9.The officers of the Corps shall be appointed by theSecretary to the Ministry of the Minister."
