    "chunk_text": "(2) (a) All proceedings instituted in any court or tribunalby or against the Sri Lanka Railways Authority establishedunder the repealed Act and pending on the day preceding thedate of commencement of this Act, shall be deemed, witheffect from the date of commencement of this Act, to beproceedings instituted by or against the Railways Departmentand be proceeded with accordingly.\n\nRepeal of Act, No.60 of 1993.\n\nTransitionalprovisions.\n\n2Sri Lanka Railways Authority (Repeal)Act, No. 3 of 2005\n\nRevocation ofparagraph (1) ofthe Order madeunder section 1 ofthe Sri LankaRailways AuthorityAct No. 60 of1993.\n\n4.From and after the date of commencement of this Act,the provisions of the Railways Ordinance (Chapter 200) andthe State Lands (Recovery of Possession) Act, No. 7 of 1979shall for all purposes, be deemed to be and to have been, inoperation as if the same had not been amended by the SriLanka Railways Authority Act, No. 60 of 1993 and shallcontinue to be the law governing the subject of Railways.\n\n5.Paragraph (1) of the Order made under section 1 of theSri Lanka Railways Authority Act, No. 60 of 1993 andpublished in Gazette Extraordinary No. 1298/22 of23.07.2003 is hereby revoked.\n\n6.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nThe State Lands(Recovery ofPossession) Act,No. 7 of 1979 andthe RailwaysOrdinance(Chapter 200)deemed to havebeen in operation.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in case ofinconsistency.\n\nSri Lanka Railways Authority (Repeal)Act, No. 3 of 20053\n\nAnnual subscription of English Bills and Acts of the Parliament Rs. 885 (Local), Rs. 1,180(Foreign), payable to the SUPERINTENDENT, GOVERNM ENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, NO. 32, TRANSWORKS HOUSE,LOTUS ROAD, COLOMBO 01 before 15th December each year in respect of the year following."
